    "difficultyReason": "Part a is scaffolded: the student tests five given square numbers for divisibility into 450, which is routine checking. Part b says 'hence', so the student picks the largest square factor (225) and applies sqrt(225)×sqrt(2). This is one direct decision with no open search, so it is easier than p22-q2, where the student must generate other factorisations unaided. It is slightly harder than a single-step recall or calculation because of the two linked parts.",
